# Privacy Policy — YouTube Night Block

**Effective date:** 12 August 2026

## Summary

YouTube Night Block does not collect, transmit, or sell any data. It makes no
network requests of its own, contains no analytics or tracking code, and
communicates with no servers. Everything it stores stays in your browser, on
your device.

## What the extension stores

The following is saved locally using `chrome.storage.local` and is never
transmitted anywhere:

- **Your schedule** — the start and end times of the blocking window
- **Your matching settings** — the regular expression pattern and flags used to
  decide which tabs get reloaded
- **A record of the most recent run** — a timestamp, whether blocking is
  currently active, and the *number* of tabs that were reloaded

The last-run record contains no URLs, page titles, or browsing history — only a
count. Removing the extension deletes all of this.

## What the extension reads but does not store

To decide which tabs to reload when the blocking window begins, the extension
reads the URLs of your open tabs and tests them against your pattern. This
happens in memory, at that moment only. Tab URLs are never written to storage,
never logged, and never sent anywhere.

## How blocking works

Blocking is performed by Chrome's `declarativeNetRequest` API using a static
rule list bundled inside the extension. Chrome applies these rules itself and
does not report back which requests matched. The extension therefore receives no
information about which sites you visit or which requests were blocked.

## Permissions

| Permission | Why it is needed |
|---|---|
| `declarativeNetRequest` | Blocks requests to YouTube domains while the scheduled window is active |
| `tabs` | Reads open tab URLs to find the ones matching your pattern, so they can be reloaded |
| `storage` | Saves your schedule and matching settings on your device |
| `alarms` | Triggers the start and end of the blocking window |

The extension requests no host permissions and cannot read the contents of any
web page.

## Third parties

None. The extension contains no analytics, no advertising, no remote code
execution, and no third-party services. No data is shared, sold, or transferred
to anyone, for any purpose.

